        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wilsonville%2C_Oregon",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The historic Boones Ferry once crossed the Willamette River, linking the two sides of what is now Wilsonville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wilsonville%2C_Oregon",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1939 a fire gutted the wooden trestle of the Oregon Electric Railway bridge over the Willamette.",
